+## Troubleshooting and compatibility
+
+- **Only the colors changed:** the extension is missing, waiting for APIs, or
+  failed during startup. With the updated package, run the installer again to
+  enable both `liquid-touch.js` and `expose_apis` and rebuild preprocessing.
+  Update an older Spicetify first using its own update command/package manager.
+- **Startup panel appears:** it identifies missing APIs, missing CSS, or the
+  actual exception. Tap **Copy details** and paste the result into this chat.
+  After the missing dependency becomes available, tap **Retry**.
+- **No startup panel or touch controls at all:** check `spicetify config extensions`
+  contains `liquid-touch.js`; confirm the matching file exists in the Extensions
+  directory beside the config file reported by `spicetify -c`.
+- **Library is incomplete:** tap Refresh in Library. The main collection API is
+  paginated; older versions try separate playlist/album/artist filters, then the
+  rootlist and visible sidebar. When only sidebar data is available, the page
+  says so. Desktop interface keeps access to Spotify’s full library.
+- **Progress works but Now Playing has no title/art:** this release reads the
+  live player state first, with wrapper, platform, event, and native-widget fallbacks.
+- **System window buttons are visible:** the native bridge is unavailable or
+  rejected a command. Space is reserved so it cannot cover touch controls. Use
+  **Glass window buttons** in settings to select system controls deliberately.
+- **Blank native pages in 1.2.0:** update both CSS and the extension together.
+  1.2.0 accidentally hid `.Root__top-container`, which also contains native search
+  and detail views. 1.3.0 keeps that parent visible and measurable.
+- **Large text needs more scrolling:** this is expected. Font size and interface
+  size are separate so you can enlarge text without enlarging every control.
+- **A Spotify update broke the layout:** update Spicetify for that client and run
+  `spicetify restore backup apply` if its existing backup is still present.
+  Use Ctrl + Alt + T for desktop access while diagnosing.
+- **Player does not cover the monitor:** maximize Spotify first. Now Playing
+  covers the full app window without changing display fullscreen.
+- **Changes to controls seem ignored:** test without other player/sidebar
+  replacement extensions. The installer deliberately preserves them.
+- **Need diagnostics:** in Spotify DevTools, run `LiquidTouch.diagnostics()`.
+  It reports version, screen area, preferences, and whether native views were
+  found. It does not collect account tokens or listening history.
+
+### What has actually been tested
+
+The supplied checks exercise the actual extension in Chromium against the
+included offline Spotify host fixture: responsive layouts, minimum touch
+targets, player actions, local keyboard, encoded search, navigation, gestures,
+restrictions, safe metadata rendering, persistence, teardown, and recovery.
+Installer tests use an isolated fake CLI and temporary configs to verify copies,
+backups, reinstallation, and restoration.
+
+**A live Spotify client and physical touchscreen were not available here.**
+This is an installable release, not a claim of verified compatibility with
+every Spotify build. Spotify's internal DOM and APIs can change. In particular,
+library API shapes, native search/track hooks, native window controls, and
+physical touch behavior need a check on your mini PC. Windows scripts are unchanged and were not rerun in this build. Earlier validation
+used PowerShell 7 on Linux against a fake CLI. Windows 5.1,
+the optional Windows COM startup-shortcut branch, and live Spotify patching
+still need a Windows machine. The manual install path is available as well.
+
