+## Listening history and updates
+
+History is stored locally in a stable IndexedDB database for the current Spotify
+profile. Settings use the same preference key across releases. Normal LiquidTouch
+updates preserve both, along with lyric timing and the update-feed URL. Existing
+local history is imported automatically. Browser/Spotify profile data removal,
+changing profiles or reinstalling Spotify with data removal can erase local data;
+this is not a cloud backup.
+
+Choose **Unlimited** in Settings → History & help to keep plays until you clear
+history yourself. With a saved-song limit (100–10,000 plays), new plays replace
+the oldest after the limit is met. Selecting a smaller limit removes the oldest
+excess records. Increasing the limit cannot recover plays already removed. Both
+Settings and the history page have **Clear history…**, followed by confirmation.
+Storage failures show a message and do not silently prune saved history.
+
+Hold a card, song row, history entry or the player artwork for 550 ms to open
+LiquidTouch’s context menu. Right-click or Shift+F10 also works. Movement cancels
+the hold. Radio, Queue, editable-playlist selection, library actions, Open and
+Copy link appear where appropriate. Devices and Queue open in LiquidTouch sheets;
+Spotify account/device restrictions are reported inside those sheets.
+
