+### New in v1.9.5
+
+With lyrics off, controls are vertically centered beside the artwork and the title
+and artist are centered in their column. History search uses the shared local
+keyboard when enabled; Enter hides that keyboard without navigating away.
+
+Tab and Back swipes reveal the actual destination UI while dragging. Sheet
+closing reveals the page below, nested context-menu Back reveals the previous
+menu, and Quick Search previews its field before opening. Short/cancelled swipes
+return; saved thresholds and animation speeds still apply. Inert incoming previews
+have bounded content and do not intercept taps or duplicate element IDs.
+
+Hold menus animate beside the selected card/artwork, or dock at the bottom on
+narrow screens. **Go to song radio** resolves Spotify’s generated playlist and
+starts it with the selected track. First-session full/quick searches keep a local
+route, ignore stale startup navigation and retry failed requests once.
+
+**Appearance & glass → Low-RAM mode** reduces LiquidTouch’s caches, preloading,
+artwork concurrency and image/blur effects. The touch interface remains usable;
+some pages may reload. History and settings stay saved. This does not promise a
+fixed reduction in Spotify’s total process memory. Disable it for full effects.
