+# Validation — LiquidTouch v1.9.6
+
+Build `2026-11-03-qol`, checked 3 November 2026.
+
+## Current acceptance checks
+
+- **14 Chromium browser suites passed** (`tests/release-196.cjs`) using the generated production extension and CSS in the offline Spotify host. Browser: Chromium 153.0.8010.0; trusted CDP touch input was used for swipes.
+- Coverage includes hidden/loading/unavailable lyrics, current-song-only auto-show, stale lyric responses, manual empty-pane display, per-song Off, manual lookup with auto-Off, migration of the old global flag, every Settings range in 5% steps, physical-value conversion and reload persistence.
+- Home checks cover live playlist/album/artist ordering and a native recommendation snapshot being reordered with a removed card. Gesture checks cover tabs, edge Back, player-wide track swipes, Settings Back, Quick Search from below the toolbar, sheet content pulls and retaining list scrolling in both normal and Low-RAM modes.
+- Low-RAM checks verify 24 initially rendered library cards, expansion to 48 using Show more, **zero full player-control paints for 20 unchanged playback events**, no decorative Element.animate calls, no background image resource and immediate play/pause state updates. These are host-contract/render-work checks, not a measurement of total live Spotify RAM or frame rate.
+- Player layout was checked at 1024 x 600 with the reported 130% text / 120% interface scales. The artwork shortcut is absent and the artwork-size control remains available in Settings. The lyrics-off deck is centered.
+- The **actual v1.9.6 update JSON** was imported into the actual revised **v1.9.5** loader. The new runtime mounted, migrated preferences to percentage steps, retained local listening history and text/interface scales, created one shell, and reloaded from its verified runtime cache.
+- **12 retained simulated-host search/keyboard/artwork regression suites passed** (`tests/revised-195.cjs`). These use the production controller and cover full/Quick client/native recovery, stale searches, errors/empty results, repeated Backspace and release/cancel/Unicode behavior, and artwork drag prevention.
+- **7 Python installer tests passed** (`tests/test_installer.py`) against the real Linux/macOS installer helpers and an isolated fake Spicetify CLI. Installer source scripts remain unchanged.
+- Six real-music gallery captures completed without page errors. Their public music metadata and artwork remain unchanged. Gallery playback is simulated; no audio or real lyric text is supplied.
+- JavaScript/Bash syntax, generated loader/runtime/source matching, runtime integrity, feed/package checksums, ZIP CRC, and the final standalone Git bundle are checked during packaging.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+Install Playwright and Sharp, provide a compatible local Chromium executable using
+`LT_CHROME`, then run:
+
+```bash
+node tools/build-preview.cjs
+LT_OLD_PREVIEW=/path/to/revised-v1.9.5/LiquidTouch-Preview.html node tests/release-196.cjs
+node tests/revised-195.cjs
+python3 tests/test_installer.py
+node tools/build-preview.cjs --gallery
+node tools/capture-gallery.cjs
+```
+
+Without `LT_OLD_PREVIEW`, the 13 current-runtime browser suites run and the actual
+old-runtime update suite is omitted. Historical `release-*.cjs` files retain
+version-specific expectations; they are not a blanket v1.9.6 acceptance command.
+Exploratory runs of `ui.cjs` stopped at its old arbitrary 27% volume expectation
+(now constrained to 5% steps), and `release-195.cjs` stopped at an older search
+failure expectation that predates the revised native-view recovery. Those full
+historical runs are not counted as passes above.
+
+## Limits
+
+No signed-in Windows Spotify session or physical touchscreen was available.
+Native service responses are simulated; API compatibility, actual mini-PC input
+feel and live CPU/GPU/RAM use still need confirmation on the user's system.
+Windows PowerShell installers were unchanged and were not rerun for v1.9.6.
+The reductions in DOM, image sampling, effects, polling and duplicate painting
+are concrete; they cannot guarantee that Spotify itself will be lag-free.
+
+The notes below belong to earlier releases and are retained as history.
 
